---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---

<Legal title="Refund Policy" description="Refunds, cancellations and access issues for Dima Publishing purchases." updated="October 10, 2026">
  <p>
    We want you to be happy with what you buy from us. If something isn’t right, tell us and we will fix it or give your
    money back.
  </p>

  <h2>Digital books and individual access</h2>
  <p>
    You can request a full refund within <strong>14 days</strong> of purchase for any individual digital book or reader
    access. Just email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> with the email address you used to buy and your
    order details. Once a refund is issued, access to the purchased content ends.
  </p>

  <h2>Subscriptions and renewals</h2>
  <p>
    If a product renews automatically, you can cancel at any time and you will keep access until the end of the period
    you already paid for. If you are charged for a renewal you didn’t mean to keep, contact us within 14 days of the
    renewal date for a full refund of that renewal.
  </p>

  <h2>Course, department and campus licenses</h2>
  <p>
    Institutional purchases are governed by the agreement or quote signed with your institution, including its
    cancellation and refund terms. Contact us if you need to change seat counts or terms mid-term.
  </p>

  <h2>Technical problems</h2>
  <p>
    If you can’t access something you paid for, contact us first. We will try to fix it quickly, and if we can’t, we
    will refund you in full regardless of the 14-day window.
  </p>

  <h2>How refunds are paid</h2>
  <p>
    Refunds go back to the original payment method through Stripe. They usually appear within 5–10 business days,
    depending on your bank.
  </p>

  <h2>Questions</h2>
  <p>Email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> or use our <a href="/contact/?topic=support">contact form</a>.</p>
</Legal>
